button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-364","With Start Playback with Record on in the Record, Warp & Launch Settings, recording starts when the button is pressed; otherwise it waits for Play or a launched Session clip. Shift-click does the opposite.",["Arrangement Record button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-573","Behavior — toggle.",["Arrangement Record button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-601","Remote control — MIDI or key mapping. Launchpad/Custom/Available/1-Arrangement maps a Launchpad pad to it.",["Arrangement Record button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-721","Source",["Arrangement Record button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-734","Ableton/Live/UG/19 Recording New Clips/03 Recording/01 Recording Into the Arrangement · 19.3.1 Recording Into the Arrangement",["Arrangement Record button","Source"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record/","source-block-966","Ableton/Live/UG/07 Session View/05 Recording Sessions into the Arrangement · 7.5 Recording Sessions into the Arrangement",["Arrangement Record button","Source"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-82","Automation Arm button",[]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-108","Enables recording of mixer and device parameter changes as automation in Session clips or Arrangement tracks, and tempo changes in the Arrangement.",["Automation Arm button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-377","Behavior — toggle: on enables automation recording; off disables automation recording.",["Automation Arm button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-473","Values — on or off.",["Automation Arm button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-502","In Arrangement View, enable Automation Arm and start Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Arrangement-Record. Manual changes to tempo, mixer and device parameters are recorded on all tracks; individual track arming is unnecessary for automation.",["Automation Arm button"]],["Ableton/Live/UI/Control-Bar/Button/Automation-Arm/","source-block-753","In Session View, enable Automation Arm, arm the tracks and start Session Record to record mixer and device changes into clips. Setting Record Session automation in to All Tracks records into all playing clips, regardless of track arming.",["Automation Arm button"]]],"format_version":5}